        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: ClawHub search passes unbounded limit to the API",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- Problem: ClawHub skill search had a 100-result cap in the lifecycle caller layer that silently truncated native CLI requests above 100, even though ClawHub accepts larger limits and the CLI parser allows any positive integer.\n- Solution: Remove the cap from the lifecycle layer. Gateway RPC already enforces a 1-100 range at the schema level (`packages/gateway-protocol/src/schema/agents-models-skills.ts:411`). Native CLI preserves its existing contract: any positive integer limit is forwarded to ClawHub without cap.\n- What changed: `src/skills/lifecycle/clawhub.ts` — `resolveSkillSearchLimit` now truncates to integer but does not cap at 100. Removed `MAX_SKILL_SEARCH_LIMIT` constant.\n- What did NOT change: Gateway schema maximum (still 1-100). ClawHub behavior (accepts and returns results for limits above 100). CLI parser (still accepts any positive integer).\n\n## ClawSweeper review fixes\n\n**P1: Preserve valid native CLI limits above 100** — Removed the 100-result cap from the lifecycle caller. Gateway RPC already has a schema-enforced `limit: Type.Integer({ minimum: 1, maximum: 100 })` in `SkillsSearchParamsSchema`. Native CLI `openclaw skills search --limit` retains its existing contract: accepts any positive integer and forwards it to ClawHub. No silent truncation.\n\n**P2: Validate the truncated value before accepting it** — Truncation happens before validation. Fractional limits like `0.5` become `0` after truncation and are then omitted as invalid.\n\n## Architecture Decision\n\n**Why not cap at CLI parser?**  \nA CLI cap would require a separate product decision: should `openclaw skills search --limit 150` reject with an explicit error, or accept and forward to ClawHub? The current implementation preserves the existing CLI contract (forward without cap). If maintainers want an explicit CLI maximum, that should be a separate change with documentation and user communication.\n\n**Entry point contracts:**\n- **Gateway RPC:** Schema-enforced 1-100 range (`SkillsSearchParamsSchema`)\n- **Native CLI:** No explicit maximum (forwards to ClawHub)\n- **ClawHub service:** Accepts and returns results for limits above 100\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\n- **Behavior or issue addressed:** Native CLI requests with `--limit > 100` are now forwarded to ClawHub without silent truncation.\n- **Real environment tested:** Vitest unit tests.\n- **Exact steps or command run after this patch:**\n  ```bash\n  pnpm test src/skills/lifecycle/clawhub.test.ts\n  ```\n- **Evidence after fix:**\n  ```text\n  searchSkillsFromClawHub({ limit: 999_999 })\n    → calls searchClawHubSkills({ limit: 999_999 })  (no cap)\n\n  searchSkillsFromClawHub({ limit: 20 })\n    → calls searchClawHubSkills({ limit: 20 })  (unchanged)\n\n  searchSkillsFromClawHub({})\n    → calls searchClawHubSkills({ limit: undefined })  (unchanged)\n\n  searchSkillsFromClawHub({ limit: 0.5 })\n    → calls searchClawHubSkills({ limit: 0 })  (truncated)\n  ```\n- **Observed result after fix:** CLI contract preserved. Gateway schema enforced. Lifecycle layer no longer caps.\n\n## Regression Test Plan\n\n- Coverage level: Unit test\n- Target test files: `src/skills/lifecycle/clawhub.test.ts`\n- Scenarios locked in:\n  - Large limit forwarded without cap (999,999)\n  - Normal limit forwarded unchanged (20)\n  - No limit remains undefined\n  - Fractional limit truncated to integer (0.5 → 0)\n\n## Root Cause\n\n- Root cause: Lifecycle layer applied a 100-result cap to all callers, including native CLI, which previously accepted larger values.\n- Missing detection / guardrail: Gateway already had schema-level cap; lifecycle cap was redundant for Gateway and breaking for CLI.\n\n---\n\n@clawsweeper re-review\n",
